Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

S-NSSAI Slice Differentiator (SD) has a reserved value 0xFFFFFF meaning
"no SD value associated with the SST" (TS 24.501 Section 9.11.2.8). A
previous change removed the filter for this reserved value, causing it
to be passed to the NetworkSliceInfo Builder, which throws
IllegalArgumentException because the value exceeds the maximum allowed
value (0xFFFFFE). This crashes the process. Fix this by mapping 0xFFFFFF
back to no-slice (-1). Also wrap the payload processing in a try-catch
block and add null-safety checks to prevent future crashes from parsing
exceptions.

Bug: 517377034
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Test: atest NetworkSliceSelectionAssistanceInformationTest EpdgTunnelManagerTest
